env/
jobs/
checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pt
.DS_Store
.venv/
node_modules/
*.mp4
!docs/*.mp4
!bench/*.mp4
# the suites' default input: `node verify.mjs` with no arguments has to work
# from a fresh clone, so the 5 s parkour clip and its first frame are here.
!sample.mp4
# the landing hero's "before" half: 75 KB of the same clip, cropped and cut to
# the dots' own time base. The page is nothing without it.
!web/demo/demo-before.mp4
bench/_res/
.claude/

# Regenerable binaries for the browser engine. `setup.sh` writes both:
#   web/models/*.onnx  <- onnxexport/export_onnx.py   (~130 MB)
#   web/ort/           <- npm i onnxruntime-web       (~41 MB)
# web/models/manifest.json and web/models/consts.bin ARE committed: they are
# small and the page needs them to know what it is missing. The same holds for
# the other two tracker resolutions under web/models/512/ and web/models/1024/
# -- their manifests are committed, their graphs are not.
web/models/*.onnx
web/models/*/*.onnx
web/ort/

# release tarballs built by tools/build-models-release.sh
dist/

# verify-web.mjs re-exports these on every run; the screenshots are the evidence
docs/w-*-export.*
# the decode flow builds a cue-less WebM and a 90 s MP4 with ffmpeg and removes
# them again; they are here so an interrupted run does not leave them tracked
docs/w-decode-camera-like.webm
docs/w-decode-long.mp4
# the matched-cut runs write both halves of the pair and the frames they were
# checked against. Regenerable, and the numbers live in the reports.
docs/o-original-cut.mp4
docs/w-original-cut.webm
docs/w-original-dithered.webm
docs/w-original-ref-*.png
# the canvas run's 9:16 pair in the tab — regenerable, and the numbers are in
# the report; the contact sheets beside them are the evidence and stay
docs/w-canvas-916-dithered.webm
docs/w-canvas-916-original.webm
# the anchored-camera run's 9:16 pair, same reasoning: the screenshots under
# docs/ux-after/follow-*.png are the evidence and the numbers are in the report
docs/w-follow-anchor.webm
# the range run's pair and its reference frames, same reasoning
docs/w-range-dithered.webm
docs/w-range-original.webm
docs/w-range-ref-*.png
docs/w-range-dots.gz
docs/seq-item-look-*.dots.gz
docs/seq-item-look.mp4
docs/seq-particle.dots.gz
docs/seq-particle.mp4
